{
  "requirement": "`fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents. `format` renders that same value for the agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    fn fingerprint(&self) -> Fingerprint;\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.NodeContents` has three obligations: `fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents, `format` renders that same value, and the trait is `Send + Sync`. Both marked tests are in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs`, and together they cover all three.\n\n- **Fingerprint identifies the version.**\n  - `structural_fingerprint_example_tracks_the_selected_function` asserts that a reformatted function has an equal fingerprint (`assert_eq!`). It asserts that a changed function has a different fingerprint (`assert_ne!`).\n  - `selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits` asserts that the fingerprint equals the earlier value after the source handle is dropped and the file is edited.\n  - It also asserts the fingerprint's value and scheme.\n- **Format renders that same value.**\n  - In `selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits`, `format()` equals \"second\" before and after the file edit. This is the same retained contents the unchanged fingerprint identifies, so `format` does not reread external state.\n  - In `structural_fingerprint_example_tracks_the_selected_function`, `format()` is asserted exactly for the original, reformatted and changed variants. The reformatted variant has the same fingerprint but its own rendering. The changed variant has a different fingerprint and a different rendering. So format and fingerprint stay aligned with the contents.\n- **`Send + Sync`.** The same test calls `shareable(&original as &dyn NodeContents)` with `T: Send + Sync + ?Sized`, which checks the bound through the trait object. `contracts.rs` also has a `check_bounds` helper, `contents<T: NodeContents + Send + Sync>`.\n\n`public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `tests/public_api.rs` covers the trait's public export and signature inventory. No obligation is untested, and I found no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
  "references": "ff7f8c7a0f869b145ff5b5e624138875b722c311265bb2e0679a5730d4e14c33",
